        <h1 id="introduction">Introduction</h1>
<p>API Documentation for Gấu Phim Movie Booking System</p>
<aside>
    <strong>Base URL</strong>: <code>http://localhost:5000</code>
</aside>
<pre><code>    # GẤU PHIM API DOCUMENTATION

    Welcome to the Gấu Phim API documentation. This API powers the movie booking system.

    ## 🔐 Authentication

    Most endpoints require authentication using JWT Bearer token.</code></pre>
<p>To get a token, use the <code>/api/login</code> endpoint.</p>
<h2 id="base-url">📋 Base URL</h2>
<p>All API endpoints are prefixed with <code>/api/</code></p>
<h2 id="response-format">📦 Response Format</h2>
<p>All responses are in JSON format with appropriate HTTP status codes.</p>
<h2 id="rate-limiting">🔄 Rate Limiting</h2>
<p>API requests are rate limited to 60 requests per minute per IP.</p>
<aside>
💡 You can test endpoints directly using the "Try It Out" button on each endpoint.
</aside>

        <h1 id="authenticating-requests">Authenticating requests</h1>
<p>To authenticate requests, include an <strong><code>Authorization</code></strong> header with the value <strong><code>"Bearer Bearer {your_jwt_token_here}"</code></strong>.</p>
<p>All authenticated endpoints are marked with a <code>requires authentication</code> badge in the documentation below.</p>
<p>To authenticate API requests, you need to include a JWT token in the <code>Authorization</code> header.</p>
<p><strong>How to get your token:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Call the <code>/api/login</code> endpoint with your credentials</li>
<li>Copy the <code>token</code> from the response</li>
<li>Include it in subsequent requests as: <code>Authorization: Bearer {token}</code></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> Tokens expire after 24 hours.</p>

        <h1 id="authentication">Authentication</h1>

    <p>APIs for user authentication, registration, and Google OAuth login.</p>

                                <h2 id="authentication-POSTapi-register">Register a new user</h2>

<p>
</p>

<p>Create a new user account with the provided information.</p>

<span id="example-requests-POSTapi-register">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request POST \
    "http://localhost:5000/api/register" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --data "{
    \"FullName\": \"Nguyễn Văn A\",
    \"Email\": \"user@example.com\",
    \"Password\": \"123456\",
    \"PhoneNumber\": \"0987654321\",
    \"Gender\": \"Male\",
    \"DateOfBirth\": \"2000-01-01\",
    \"RoleId\": 17,
    \"Status\": \"Inactive\"
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:5000/api/register"
);

const headers = {
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};

let body = {
    "FullName": "Nguyễn Văn A",
    "Email": "user@example.com",
    "Password": "123456",
    "PhoneNumber": "0987654321",
    "Gender": "Male",
    "DateOfBirth": "2000-01-01",
    "RoleId": 17,
    "Status": "Inactive"
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "POST",
    headers,
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>


<div class="php-example">
    <pre><code class="language-php">$client = new \GuzzleHttp\Client();
$url = 'http://localhost:5000/api/register';
$response = $client-&gt;post(
    $url,
    [
        'headers' =&gt; [
            'Content-Type' =&gt; 'application/json',
        ],
        'json' =&gt; [
            'FullName' =&gt; 'Nguyễn Văn A',
            'Email' =&gt; 'user@example.com',
            'Password' =&gt; '123456',
            'PhoneNumber' =&gt; '0987654321',
            'Gender' =&gt; 'Male',
            'DateOfBirth' =&gt; '2000-01-01',
            'RoleId' =&gt; 17,
            'Status' =&gt; 'Inactive',
        ],
    ]
);
$body = $response-&gt;getBody();
print_r(json_decode((string) $body));</code></pre></div>


<div class="python-example">
    <pre><code class="language-python">import requests
import json

url = 'http://localhost:5000/api/register'
payload = {
    "FullName": "Nguyễn Văn A",
    "Email": "user@example.com",
    "Password": "123456",
    "PhoneNumber": "0987654321",
    "Gender": "Male",
    "DateOfBirth": "2000-01-01",
    "RoleId": 17,
    "Status": "Inactive"
}
headers = {
  'Content-Type': 'application/json'
}

response = requests.request('POST', url, headers=headers, json=payload)
response.json()</code></pre></div>

